  pub let ks_op_set_raw : (u64, u64) -> u64 !{mem, sysreg} @{cap} =
    fn (session_id: u64) (flags: u64) -> unsafe {
      effects: {mem, sysreg}, capabilities: {cap},
      justification: "R127.M3 (paideia-os #2599): translate R127.M3's _shell_session_set_raw return band to the KS_* band. SS_RAW_OK -> KS_OK; SS_ERR_BAD_ID (0x1102) -> KS_ERR_BAD_SESSION (0x1110); SS_RAW_ERR_BAD_FLAGS (0x1105) -> KS_ERR_BAD_OP (0x1111); other non-zero -> KS_ERR_BAD_SESSION defensively. Bumps KS_ST_SET_RAW_OK (slot 8) on success / KS_ST_REFUSED (slot 6) on either error. Two callee-save pushes (rbx=session_id, r12=flags) + sub rsp,8 pad land rsp%16==0 at every nested call. Shape parallels ks_op_set_state one-for-one. Labels prefixed ks_sr_.",
      block: {
